# Docker build-context excludes (M10, sprints#58).
#
# Dockerfile:31 (`COPY . .`, ahead of `buf generate` regenerating gen/go and `go build
# ./cmd/delightd`) had no .dockerignore behind it: the full .git history and the live
# .env (gitignored, not dockerignored -- two different exclude lists) both landed in the
# builder layer and the BuildKit cache.
#
# The image build needs: go.mod/go.sum, cmd/, pkg/, proto/ + buf.gen.go.yaml + buf.yaml
# (buf generate's inputs), kube/, delight.yaml, mcp.json, meubilair.yaml (the config
# templates baked into /etc/delightd -- see Dockerfile's ARG GIT_SHA stage), and
# scripts/ (the host wrapper; kept in the context even though this Dockerfile does not
# read it today, so adding a stage that does never needs a dockerignore review first).
# Everything below is excluded because no Dockerfile stage reads it. Anchored to the
# context root (leading /) -- no bare/glob patterns matching at arbitrary depth, except
# the one deliberate env-overlay wildcard below.

# Secrets / per-workstation config -- never in a layer or the BuildKit cache. .env is
# gitignored already; dockerignore is the separate list docker actually consults.
/.env
/.env.*
!/.env.example

# Full history: the image never needs a single commit, and .git is a moving target that
# would bust the COPY layer cache on every commit even when no tracked file changed.
/.git/

# Agent tooling -- never shipped in any artifact.
/.claude/

# Build/test/runtime artifacts that land in the repo root by accident, not by design
# (already gitignored; dockerignored here too since gitignore and dockerignore are
# independent lists).
/bin/
/coverage.out
/coverage.out.tmp
/traefik.json

# Regenerated in-image by `buf generate --template buf.gen.go.yaml` (Dockerfile). A
# stale local gen/go would be silently overwritten at best, or leave orphaned files at
# worst if a message was removed since the last local `task generate`. gen/rust (the
# committed serde crate) is Rust-only and unused by this Go build.
/gen/

# Test source and fixtures: `go build ./cmd/delightd` never compiles these, only
# `go test` does, and that runs outside the image (see the M10/M11 gates in
# sprints#58: go test ./... and -tags=integration ./test/integration/... both run on
# the host, against the built binary or a running container, never inside a build).
/test/
/tests/

# CI/dev tooling with no runtime role in the image.
/.github/
/.githooks/
